Let me examine the `vflip_process` and `mp_image_from_av_frame` for potential issues.

In `vflip_process`, when the format/vflip matches the cached values, it sets `img->params.vflip = p->target_vflip`. But when a vflip filter was successfully created, `p->target_vflip = 0`, so subsequent frames get `vflip = 0`, which is correct. When no filter (VO handles it or vflip==0), `target_vflip = vflip`, preserving it. This looks consistent.

Let me check the gpu-next distort logic and the mp_image.c side data handling more carefully.

